// Seven equal bars on a 3:5 field.
vexyl 1
meta {
  name "Girlflux flag"
  designer "Mod Hermy (Pride-Flags, DeviantArt)"
  encoder "Naomi Persephone Amethyst"
  license "CC-BY-SA-4.0"
  render-license "CC0-1.0"
  date "2017-01-19"
  source "https://www.deviantart.com/pride-flags/art/Girlflux-Womanflux-3-658394567"
  source "https://lgbtqia.fandom.com/wiki/Genderflux"
  note "Defining source: 'Girlflux / Womanflux (3)' by Pride-Flags on DeviantArt, published 2017-01-19 (read). Its description says the flag was 'Designed by Mod Hermy (chosen from my flag scraps folder by anonymous)' and that the term was coined by kitsuneshay-blog. The post gives no color meanings, hex values or proportion. The boyflux flag of 8 February 2017 is its counterpart."
  note "Construction and colors are read from the post's image (5000 by 3000 PNG): seven bars of 429, 426, 433, 424, 433, 426 and 429 pixels, taken as equal, #f9e6d6, #f3526c, #c00310, #e9c587, #c00310, #f3526c, #f9e6d6. This is my sampling, not hex the designer gave. The 3:5 proportion is the image's."
}
palette {
  cream "#f9e6d6"
  pink "#f3526c"
  red "#c00310"
  gold "#e9c587"
}
proportion hoist=3 fly=5

bars cream pink red gold red pink cream
